-# Anderson Etal 2022 NBER
+# Anderson, Hyun, and Lee (2022) NBER
 
-**Summary**: Anderson, Hyun, and Lee estimate the welfare value of South Korea's particulate-matter alert program using a fuzzy RD design at the alert-issuance threshold, and develop a revealed-preference framework in which the externalized (publicly-borne) share of avoided healthcare expenditures provides a sharp lower bound on social welfare gains (source: Anderson_etal_2022_NBER.pdf). The paper is the JMP's methodological anchor for the alert-program welfare-bound exercise (source: Anderson_etal_2022_NBER.pdf).
+**Summary**: Establishes a lower-bound welfare framework for air-quality alert systems (AQAS) using a fuzzy RD at South Korea's PM alert threshold; finds alerts reduce government-borne health expenditures by $28.6M (contemporaneous) at a benefit-cost ratio of 7:1, with effects entirely via avoidance behavior (no ambient PM change at threshold). The fiscal externality $\Delta E$ identified here enters the JMP directly as the estimable component of $\Delta W$.
 
 **Sources**: Anderson_etal_2022_NBER.pdf
 
