-The paper uses a fuzzy RD design at the South Korean PM-alert issuance threshold. The running variable is the daily maximum of 2-hour-minimum PM2.5 and PM10 readings, normalized by their respective issuance thresholds (90 µg/m³ and 150 µg/m³) and pooled via the multi-cutoff procedure of Cattaneo et al. (2020) so the cutoff sits at zero (source: Anderson_etal_2022_NBER.pdf). Assignment is fuzzy because (a) authorities also weigh weather conditions and (b) issuance and cancellation thresholds differ, so alerts persist into below-threshold days.
+Minors: ≈30% of mean below-threshold spending.
 
-The first-stage and reduced-form regressions are local-linear with population weights and a default bandwidth $h = 20$ (CCT-optimal range 17–22):
