-|---|---|---|---|---|
-| Respiratory | $-15.03$ (5.67) | $-3.78$ (2.13) | $-4.30$ (2.80) | $-5.83$ (2.50) |
-| Cardiovascular | $-0.040$ (0.035) | $-2.83$ (0.77) | $-9.64$ (3.68) | $-3.26$ (1.01) |
-
-Percentage effects (relative to mean expenditure with running variable in $[-20, 0]$): **minors respiratory $-30\%$, adults cardiovascular $-23\%$, older adults cardiovascular $-14\%$** (source: Anderson_etal_2022_NBER.pdf).
-
-Dynamic (3-day rolling sum) estimates are 2.2–2.8 times the contemporaneous coefficients (Table 6), capturing both multi-day alert episodes (mean duration 1.87 days) and some lagged avoidance benefit after alert expiry (source: Anderson_etal_2022_NBER.pdf).
-
-**Aggregate gross-benefit lower bound** (sum across diseases and ages, scaled by exposed population and the 70% public-share factor): $\Delta E \geq 28.6$ million USD (contemporaneous) or $36.7$ million USD (dynamic) over 2016–2017 (source: Anderson_etal_2022_NBER.pdf). **Alert-system operating cost** ~4 million USD over 2016–2017. **Minimum benefit-cost ratio: 7.1:1 (contemporaneous) or 9.2:1 (dynamic).**
